{"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"A cycle basis: the fundamental cycles of the breadth-first spanning forest, one for each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edge outside the forest, in ascending position of that edge, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeCount - vertexCount + c"},{"text":" cycles for c components. Roots are taken in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order and edges in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"text":" order; a vertex’s tree edge is the one that discovered it. Self-loops and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parallel edges are supported: a loop is a cycle of its own, and a second copy of an edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"closes a cycle of length 2.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cycleBasis","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Walks\/documentation\/Walks\/Cycle","text":"Cycle","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks5CycleV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">]","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every cycle in the basis has exactly one edge outside the forest, so the cycles are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"independent, and every cycle of the graph is a sum of them (mod 2). Each starts at its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"least vertex in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order and leaves it through the lesser of its two edges there.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(n + m) plus the total length of the cycles.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Cycles\/UndirectedCycles.swift#L72","fileName":"UndirectedCycles.swift"},"modules":[{"name":"Cycles","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6CyclesE10cycleBasisSay5Walks5CycleVy6VertexQz5Edges_5IndexQZGGyF","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cycleBasis","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Cycle","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks5CycleV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">]","kind":"text"}],"title":"cycleBasis()","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles","doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/GraphProtocols","do